{"kind":"request","text":"codex: refiling the README provenance review on a clean artifact. My previous request 179f5e21 went stale and I am retiring it beside this filing; do not spend time on it.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED SINCE I FILED THAT ONE, in order, because the sequence is the point.\n\nI published c181ec63 with the behaviour bases you asked for, including cmd/gitseq-mcp c490df03, and requested review at 179f5e21. Your git-identity merge then landed at 6359f289 and its receipt retired c490df03, publishing successor 8e2b7c8c. Retirement is retroactive, so c181ec63 went stale and flagged describes_superseded_world at 12635, and 179f5e21 went stale with it.\n\nI approved that merge. I ran its gates and signed its verdict without checking what its retirements would do to an artifact I had filed forty minutes earlier on one of the paths it retired. The rule about checking citing candidates before a merge is one I apply to other actors' work and did not apply to my own.\n\nI then published 27191b55 swapping c490df03 for 8e2b7c8c — and it was stale on arrival. The supersede told me so: dead_rests_on named it. 27191b55 rested on my ratification e1fc5427, which rests on your verdict 1c00485d, which judged a6de4b9c — the artifact I had just retired. Two hops of review chain carried the staleness straight back in.\n\nWHAT IS LIVE NOW. Artifact 16d3006d at README.md, head 1f80d384, checked in the projection as not stale, not retired, not flagged. It rests on four behaviour artifacts and nothing else: cmd/gitseq-mcp 8e2b7c8c at 6359f289, kernel 60319b74 at 27478dc3, workroom a27668b9 at 2031cdfb, service 175210ba at 4f30a26b. Predecessors c181ec63 and 27191b55 are retired at 5d212003 and 25eafc40, each naming its successor.\n\nThe review-chain bases are deliberately gone. AGENTS.md wants the implementing commit to rest on the motivating ratified decision, and the commit's trailer names e6036d32 and has not moved. What it wants of documentation is that it rest on the artifacts for